# The installer.
#
# `curl -fsSL https://rowel.novabox.ai/install | sh` is printed inside the app,
# on the web page, and in the README — it is the one URL that cannot be
# corrected once someone has read it. So the thing it resolves to lives here,
# in the repository, rather than as a redirect rule typed into a dashboard
# where nothing records why it exists.
#
# It points at `main` rather than a tag on purpose: the script itself installs
# a tag (`ROWEL_REF`), so the only thing following `main` here changes is the
# installer's own logic, and a broken installer must be fixable with a push.
/install  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/0x5446/rowel/main/install.sh  302

# The site is one page. These two addresses were pages of their own and are
# still in circulation — `/help` is the app's Help button and the App Store's
# support URL, `/get` is printed by the CLI — so they land on their sections.
/help  /#help  301
/get   /#get   301
